  "rewrites": {
   "1": {
    "original": "It also tends to be process-oriented at the higher level - the refactor menu in Visual Studio includes features for renaming code sections, extracting code into classes, and optimizing conditionals and loops.",
    "rewrite": "At a higher level, it often focuses on processes like those in Visual Studio\u2019s refactor menu, which offers options for renaming code sections, creating separate classes from code, and refining conditional statements and loops."
   },
   "3": {
    "original": "Extracting a simple method into a new class seems straightforward enough at the programming level, but would we even want to?",
    "rewrite": "Dividing a straightforward method into a new class appears simple enough in programming, but should we really do it?"
